.TH SESSLINT-DIFF 1 "" "SessLint 0.2.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-diff \- [read\-only] Structurally diff two session files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint diff [\-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}] [\-\-format\-a {claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}] [\-\-format\-b {claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}] [\-\-output\-format {human,json}] [\-\-json] A B
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Compare two session files by event identity (not text diff): added/removed events, kind changes, parent relinks, sequence reorders, content changes (hash only).
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B A
Path to the first session file
.TP
.B B
Path to the second session file
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-format {auto,claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}
Session format adapter for both inputs (default: auto) Choices: auto, claude\-code\-jsonl, openai\-agents, codex\-rollout, canonical. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-format\-a {claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}
Format override for input A only Choices: claude\-code\-jsonl, openai\-agents, codex\-rollout, canonical.
.TP
.B \-\-format\-b {claude\-code\-jsonl,openai\-agents,codex\-rollout,canonical}
Format override for input B only Choices: claude\-code\-jsonl, openai\-agents, codex\-rollout, canonical.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-format {human,json}
Output format (default: human) Choices: human, json.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit sesslint.diff/v1 JSON (shortcut for \-\-output\-format json)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

